WEBVTT

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.165
Welcome to Alaventra. Rank in
search. Get recommended by AI.

00:00:06.143 --> 00:00:10.493
In tutorial 6.1, you'll see every
page written for your website,

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:12.204
from the first draft to live.

00:00:13.245 --> 00:00:15.820
First, click Content in the sidebar.

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:18.859
This is where every page
written for your website lives.

00:00:19.864 --> 00:00:24.414
At the top, you see how many pages
are live and how many are waiting.

00:00:24.464 --> 00:00:29.094
Write a page starts a new one, and the
next step names the page to publish first.

00:00:30.128 --> 00:00:35.478
Next, look at the Content pipeline. Pages
written but not live yet sit on the left,

00:00:35.528 --> 00:00:37.516
and published pages on the right.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:42.732
A page that needs your edits says Needs
your edits, with See what to edit.

00:00:44.455 --> 00:00:47.680
Pages that are ready say
what they need. Ready,

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:51.530
stronger with your input means a
few questions would make it better.

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:55.431
Ready, waiting for your OK means
it only needs your approval.

00:00:56.394 --> 00:01:00.169
Each live page says Live, checked
once its address was checked,

00:01:00.219 --> 00:01:02.395
with Re-check page and Unpublish.

00:01:03.415 --> 00:01:07.365
If a page was marked published on
your word and did not match the draft,

00:01:07.415 --> 00:01:10.462
it says Not verified, so
you can check its address.

00:01:11.451 --> 00:01:15.751
The bar counts pages that are
live, waiting, or need your edits.

00:01:15.801 --> 00:01:19.562
The chips show pages from one
source, like your keyword ladders.

00:01:20.546 --> 00:01:25.621
Then click Table to see every page in rows,
with its status, the day it went live,

00:01:25.671 --> 00:01:27.443
its address and its files.

00:01:28.592 --> 00:01:31.917
Further down, choose how
many pages a week you get,

00:01:31.967 --> 00:01:34.517
check your business
profile and case studies,

00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:36.915
and test any page before you publish it.

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:42.059
Generated pages lists each
page report with its downloads.

00:01:42.109 --> 00:01:44.273
Click a page to open its report.

00:01:45.409 --> 00:01:48.859
The report shows the page's grade,
what would make it stronger,

00:01:48.909 --> 00:01:53.080
like questions to answer, and every
file, ready for you to publish.

00:01:54.121 --> 00:01:59.262
So, open Content, read the board, then
switch to the table and open a report.

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:05.850
That's every page in one place. Next,
tell Alaventra you published a page,

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:07.823
in tutorial 6.2.
